  "note": "Keyed on the attacker's STAGE and a three-tier band of its LEVEL, then the charge -- not on the level alone, which is what the table this replaced assumed. The attribute plays no part: stage 3 was read on a Data pet and a Virus pet and came out identical at every level and charge. Every stage has exactly three tiers and the top one is always the max level on its own. Read off real hardware two ways, the training minigame and map_dmx_attacks.py, agreeing on all six cells measured both. Every value is a reading: nothing here is inferred, and the three cells where two readings disagreed were settled by a re-run against the device's HP bar. Stage 1 is the one entry with a single tier: a Baby I has one level and cannot battle at all, so its row was read off the training minigame instead of the wire. It came back identical to stage 2's first tier, which is what the clamp already gave it -- so it is recorded rather than inferred, and nothing about the game changed when it went in.",
